@page "/data-deletion"
@namespace Parrot.Web.Components.Pages.Legal
@using Parrot.Web.Components.Layout.Landing
@layout LandingPageLayout

@* The reviewed Data Deletion Policy (designer, 23 November 2026), effective 19 November 2026; Meta asks for this page
   for apps that use Facebook sign-in. Changed from the document as received, as on the Privacy Policy: "yára" (it said
   "YARA CRM"), TikTok named with the other platforms, and the email is LandingCompany.Email (it was blank). *@
<LandingMetadata Title="Data Deletion Policy · yára" Description="How to ask yára to delete your personal data or your account, what can be deleted, and how we confirm it." Path="/data-deletion" />

<LandingDocument Title="Data Deletion Policy" Effective="new DateOnly(2026, 11, 19)" Updated="new DateOnly(2026, 11, 19)">
    <LandingSection Title="1. Introduction">
        <p>yára is an AI-powered customer relationship management platform that helps businesses manage customer conversations, automate interactions, and streamline communication across supported messaging channels.</p>
        <p>We respect your privacy and provide a process for requesting the deletion of personal information collected or processed through our platform.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="2. How to request data deletion">
        <p>Users and authorized business administrators may request the deletion of their personal data or yára account by:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Sending an email to <a href="mailto:@(LandingCompany.Email)?subject=Data%20Deletion%20Request%20%E2%80%93%20y%C3%A1ra">@LandingCompany.Email</a> with the subject “Data Deletion Request – yára.”</li>
            <li>Providing their registered email address and business or account name.</li>
            <li>Specifying whether they want particular information deleted or their entire account removed.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>For security purposes, we may request additional verification before processing the request.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="3. What data can be deleted?">
        <p>Depending on the request and applicable legal requirements, eligible information may include:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Personal profile and account information.</li>
            <li>Customer contact records and conversation history.</li>
            <li>AI agent configurations and automation records.</li>
            <li>Connected third-party messaging account information.</li>
            <li>Other personal data associated with the account.</li>
        </ul>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="4. Data from third-party platforms">
        <p>yára supports integrations with third-party communication platforms, including Meta services such as WhatsApp, Facebook, and Instagram, and TikTok.</p>
        <p>Users may revoke relevant permissions through the connected platform’s settings. To request deletion of information previously processed by yára, users should follow the deletion procedure above.</p>
        <p>Individuals communicating with a business through yára may also contact that business directly to exercise their privacy rights.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="5. Processing and retention">
        <p>Once a valid request is verified, yára will delete or anonymize eligible information in accordance with applicable data protection requirements.</p>
        <p>Certain records may be retained where necessary to satisfy legal obligations, prevent fraud, resolve disputes, or maintain platform security. Residual backup copies may remain temporarily until scheduled deletion.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="6. Confirmation">
        <p>We will communicate the outcome of the deletion request, including any information that must be retained and the reasons for its retention.</p>
        <p>How we handle personal information is set out in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </LandingSection>
</LandingDocument>
